<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Sicilian Kingdom of 1848</h1><p class="st-meta">1848 CE – 1849 CE · capital Palermo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The independent Sicily proclaimed in the revolution of 1848, which deposed the Bourbons and held out for sixteen months.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 12 January 1848 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Palermo</a> rose against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-of-the-two-sicilies">Ferdinand II</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-the-two-sicilies">Kingdom of the Two Sicilies</a>, one of the first revolutions of that year in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. The rebels took most of the island, revived the Sicilian constitution of 1812 and formed a government under the veteran admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruggero-settimo">Ruggero Settimo</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Sicilian parliament declared the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ile-bourbon">Bourbon</a> dynasty deposed in April 1848 and in July offered the crown to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-ferdinando-duke-of-genoa">Ferdinando, Duke of Genoa</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-albert-of-sardinia">Charles Albert</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-sardinia">Kingdom of Sardinia</a>, who declined. The state had a government, parliament and army, but was divided between moderates and radicals and lacked foreign support.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-of-the-two-sicilies">Ferdinand II</a>'s troops bombarded and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/messina">Messina</a> in September 1848. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ile-bourbon">Bourbon</a> offensive resumed in 1849, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catania">Catania</a> fell in April and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Palermo</a> surrendered in May 1849, ending the kingdom.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1848 CE – 1849 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54